--TEST--
A `set` hook's parameter type accepts the property's own type, or the hook does not compile — `rule:classes/property-hooks`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A wider parameter type compiles: an `int` value fits `?int`.
class Wider {
    public int $count {
        set (?int $v) {
            $this->count = $v ?? 0;
        }
    }

    public function constructor() {
        $this->count = 1;
    }
}

// Refused: an `int` value is not a `string`.
class Text {
    public int $count {
        set (string $v) {
            $this->count = 0;
        }
    }

    public function constructor() {
        $this->count = 42;
    }
}

// Refused: the hook gets the stored `int`, and it is not converted to `float`.
class Ratio {
    public int $count {
        set (float $v) {
            $this->count = 0;
        }
    }

    public function constructor() {
        $this->count = 42;
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: this `set` hook takes `string`, but the property is `int`
   --> case.nvs:18:14
%A
error[E0401]: this `set` hook takes `float`, but the property is `int`
   --> case.nvs:31:14
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
